## 1. Core Principles (Non-Negotiable)

### 1.1 Worker Restrictions
- **Workers do NOT initiate conversations**
- Workers only:
  - Install widgets
  - Build Google Sites only when explicitly assigned
  - Test installations
  - Reply to inbound messages (when assigned)
- **No outbound texting by workers in Phase 2**

### 1.2 Payment Model
- Workers are paid per completed job, not hourly
- No job is payable without checklist + proof

### 1.3 Scalability
- System must scale from 1 to 10+ workers without redesign

### 1.4 Channel-Centric Architecture
- **Channels — not phone numbers — are the core routing unit**
- No customer is ever "hostage" to a single phone number
- A site/widget is connected to a channel
- A channel can have:
  - Multiple texters
  - Multiple phone numbers
- Phone numbers are replaceable resources
- Texters are assignable participants

### 1.5 Message Integrity
- Every inbound customer message belongs to exactly ONE team page/channel at a time
- Messages are never shared across pages
- Team members see only their assigned pages
- Owner sees everything
- Message routing is page-centric, not user-centric

