## 2. Clarification: Onboarding vs Install Add-On vs Install Setup

**Use this section to avoid confusion between “onboarding”, “add-on”, and the install form.**

### 2.1 Post-signup onboarding

**Onboarding** = the flow a new customer goes through **after signup**. It can include:

1. **Plan selection** – Choose monthly subscription (e.g. Starter, Pro, Enterprise, or Church intro for eligible verified churches — see [Section 3.4](#34-version-1-billing-rules-client-agreed-may-2026)).
2. **Setup path (Version 1)** – Choose how to get started: **hosted link only** or **widget embed**. This is a **setup preference**, not a separate monthly product; one subscription includes both capabilities on the same site.
3. **Optional install add-on** – Choose whether to buy the one-time paid install service (see [Install add-on](#22-install-add-on) below).
4. **If they bought the add-on:** complete **install setup** (the form with website URLs, platform, install type, access method, etc.) and **SMS consent**. When that is done, we create an **Install Job** (queued for a worker).

So: onboarding is the overall “get the customer set up” flow; the **install setup form** and **SMS consent** are specific steps inside that flow when the customer has the install add-on.

### 2.2 Install add-on

The **install add-on** is an **optional one-time paid product** (not part of the monthly subscription):

- **Standard website install** (script embed): $19.99 one-time  
- **Restricted platform install** (Google Sites / iframe): $39.99 one-time  
- **Website creation / branding / multi-page build**: EXCLUDED from Phase 2 (separate future module)

- Offered **during or immediately after signup** (or at checkout), **or later from the dashboard** when a hosted-only customer requests widget installation (Version 1 — see [Section 3.4.2](#342-install-add-on--hosted-only-customers-upgrading-to-widget)).
- If the customer pays for it, they are prompted to **“Complete Setup”** (install setup + SMS consent).
- Billing stores: `install_addon_sku`, `install_addon_status` (paid | refunded | disputed), etc.

### 2.3 Install setup (the form questions)

The form in the UI (Website URL(s), Platform, Install type, Preferred placement, Access method, Notes) is **not** generic “onboarding” questions (like “company name”). It is the **install setup** step:

- **When we ask it:** Only when we will create an **Install Job** — i.e. when the customer has purchased (or will use) the **install add-on**.
- **What it collects:** Everything the worker needs to perform the install (URLs, platform, install type, how to access the site, notes).
- **Where it lives in the doc:** These fields are listed in [Section 4 – Customer Onboarding + SMS Consent Gate](#4-customer-onboarding--sms-consent-gate) as “Required Onboarding Fields” **in the sense that** they are required to complete the **install** part of onboarding (and to create the Install Job). So in short:
  - **Onboarding** = post-signup flow (plan, optional add-on, and if add-on then install setup + SMS consent).
  - **Add-on** = the paid one-time install product.
  - **Install setup form** = the questions (URLs, platform, install type, access method, notes, etc.) required for creating the Install Job; they are part of onboarding only when the customer has the add-on.

### 2.4 SMS consent

SMS consent is a **hard gate** before we create the Install Job. Customer must confirm the compliance statement (checkbox + typed text). Stored as `sms_consent_confirmed_at`. See [Section 4.2](#42-sms-consent-confirmation-hard-gate).

