## 13. Multi-User Architecture

### 12.1 Actor Definitions

#### Owner (Creator)
- Business owner account
- Full visibility across:
  - All team pages
  - All threads
  - All workers
- Can:
  - Create/edit team pages
  - Assign team members
  - Override routing
  - Escalate threads

#### Team Member
- Assigned to one or more team pages
- Can:
  - View inbox for assigned page(s)
  - Reply to assigned threads
- Cannot:
  - See other pages
  - See billing
  - Modify routing logic

#### Worker (Philippines Installer)
- Special restricted role
- Can:
  - Reply only to threads explicitly assigned
  - Install widgets
- Cannot:
  - Initiate conversations
  - See other team pages
  - See owner/team billing or settings

### 12.2 Core Entities (Conceptual Model)

#### Business (Workspace)
- `business_id`
- Owner account
- One or more team pages
- One or more Twilio numbers / messaging services

#### Team Page (Routing Destination)
A Team Page is the primary routing destination.

**Fields:**
- `team_page_id`
- `business_id`
- `name` (e.g., "Sales – Kim", "Support", "Installs")
- `assigned_user_ids[]`
- `is_active`
- `created_at`

**Rules:**
- Pages are independent inboxes
- Pages never share threads
- Pages can have multiple users
- Users can belong to multiple pages

#### Customer
- `customer_id`
- `phone_number`
- `business_id`
- `assigned_team_page_id`
- `created_at`

**Rules:**
- A customer is assigned to one page at a time
- Assignment persists until changed by Owner logic

#### Message Thread
Represents a single conversation between a customer and the business.

**Fields:**
- `thread_id`
- `customer_id`
- `team_page_id`
- `status` (open / closed / escalated)
- `last_message_at`

**Rules:**
- Threads are page-bound
- A thread cannot exist without a `team_page_id`
- Thread visibility is determined only by page assignment

#### Message
- `message_id`
- `thread_id`
- `direction` (inbound / outbound)
- `body`
- `twilio_sid`
- `delivery_status`
- `created_at`

